<!--Post: 4406--><!--Time: 1106328377-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4406"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 9:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/busters_6.html?sect=4" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve d/btk/busters_6.html?sect=4</a> <BR> <BR>&#34;In July of 1984, Investigators, set up a task force, nicknamed &#34;The Ghostbusters&#34; and hired a computer consultant to work with them in an attempt to try and discover the identity of BTK. After assembling their massive collection of DNA evidence, seven years after the last murder, investigators finished entering their data into an IBM computer, and a list of suspects began to spew out. <BR> <BR>The Ghostbusters&#34; task force discovered some of the most promising evidence during their investigation. One of the most startling clues was the revelation of one similarity, all of the murders occurred within 3 1/2 miles of one another. This led investigators to believe that the BTK strangler only felt comfortable killing in areas that were familiar to him.&#34; <BR> <BR>After 10 years, the WPD FINALLY put 2 and 2 together to figure this out and then what does the BTK do?  After almost 9 years of silence he goes and murders Vicki, who lives 6.5 miles from the prior victims.  I think this was the ONLY reason he murdered Vicki, to prove the cops wrong. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4406-->
<!--Post: 4421--><!--Time: 1106348010-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4421"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 2:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I can&#39;t believe that it actually took a team of &#34;Ghostbusters&#34; to have the revelation that the victims were within 3 1/2 miles of each other. <BR> <BR>duh  -  did they not have a map?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4421-->
<!--Post: 5369--><!--Time: 1107067077-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5369"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 10:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think the key to finding out who BTK is, lies with the Wegerle case. <BR> <BR>There was no forced entry.  Did he show up at her door with a gun, or was she familiar with him?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5369-->
<!--Post: 5414--><!--Time: 1107111873-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5414"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Angrywolf<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Angrywolf<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 11:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Doesn&#39;t mean a thing..he could have showed up wearing a uniform or saying her daughter was sick at school and she would have opened the door..then he could have pushed her back and drew his gun and taken over the situation...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5414-->
<!--Post: 5415--><!--Time: 1107112781-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5415"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 11:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Everyone in the EMS photo is wearing short sleves...it was Sept 16th...so it must have been a nice day temperature wise...perhaps she even had he door open...it looks in the pic like she had a screen door... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5415-->
<!--Post: 5432--><!--Time: 1107118154-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5432"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Where&#39;s that &#34;EMS&#34; photo at? <BR> <BR>I looked thru the linked story above but only saw a shot of her &#40;Vicki Wegerle&#41; home and a LE officer looking in/at her car... he seems to wearing a long sleeved coat perhaps a rain coat. <BR> <BR>I may have missed it?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5432-->
<!--Post: 5433--><!--Time: 1107118481-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5433"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have seen it several places but it is down the page on this link...I can&#39;t remember seening the one with the car...can your provide it?  Thanks in advance... <BR> <BR><a href="http://johnsville.blogspot.com/2004/04/btk-bind-torture-kill-strangler-info.html" target=_top>http://johnsville.blogspot.com/2004/04/btk-bind-to rture-kill-strangler-info.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5433-->
<!--Post: 5434--><!--Time: 1107118642-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5434"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It&#39;s in chapter 11 of the story link in the first post of this thread Stealth: <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolved/btk/returns_11.html?sect=4" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/serial_killers/unsolve d/btk/returns_11.html?sect=4</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5434-->
<!--Post: 5437--><!--Time: 1107119690-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5437"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 1:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No break in could mean many things.  Maybe she forgot to lock the back door, or usually did not lock it during the day &#40;the back yard is fenced with chain link&#41;. Maybe he had watched the house and noticed she left a window open on warm days. Maybe btk had learned to pick locks since his last crimes.  Maybe he had stolen her purse and copied the keys a month earlier, and so on.   <BR>Maybe she knew him, but no real reason to think so. <BR>IF it was true that the wpd did not notice how the series of crimes from 74-79 formed a pretty clear circle on a map with a diameter of about 3 miles in one part of town for several years; then btk should have stole the detectives pants while he was at it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5437-->
<!--Post: 5439--><!--Time: 1107119881-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5439"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 1:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That link has a lot of photo&#39;s I&#39;ve never seen before... good source. <BR> <BR>Interesting that the EMS is preforming CPR on Vicki Wegerle... this would imply she was killed just as the husband was coming home... when he found her... I think Den mentioned that he thought that BTK was still in the home when the husband came in and that he felt he &#40;BTK&#41; snuck out with Mr. Wegerle in the home. Of course from what I read this was all in the news reports...about her not actually being &#34;dead&#34; when the policew and EMS arrived... so it&#39;s a logical conclusion that BTK was very near and perhaps inside still. <BR> <BR>Also: the strip mall type parking lot across the  street was a easy place to watch from<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5439-->
<!--Post: 5444--><!--Time: 1107122079-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5444"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 1:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The strip mall would have been a very good place to watch...esp if you look where he parked her  car...I always assumed he had to be gone before the husband came home because he took the car and the husband would have had to park in the driveway...never saw anything to indicate the car was stolen after the husband got home...I had seen that picture...I don&#39;t know, maybe the weather changed. <BR> <BR>OK Mike - LOL...maybe he did and they are holding that back too! <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5444-->
<!--Post: 5743--><!--Time: 1107316965-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5743"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dorothy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dorothy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 8:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The Wegerle&#39;s lived in the Indian Hills Apts at 2734 W. 13th about 3 years before they moved into the house at 2404.  If you look at a map, these apts are only 1/10 mile from where her car was found. <BR> <BR>I think it&#39;s possible BTK lived in that same apartment building and knew her from there. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5743-->
<!--Post: 6565--><!--Time: 1107892997-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6565"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Neechi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Neechi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 12:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was just going to mention that at the time when Mrs. Wegerle was killed it was the standard procedure of emergency crews to ALWAYS attempt CPR on any patient.  So the fact that the picture showed them performing CPR shouldn&#39;t be used as a time of death indicator.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6565-->
